From 8a01227d1f1b770cd5c7a00dd3c9745a15e82014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:24:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] 031 (TKFillet): no empty obstacle curve after StartSol
 finds no arc on the neighbour face

ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol, the branch where the fillet runs into an arc of the
neighbour face (c1obstacle): when that arc is not found among the edges of the
neighbour face, StartSol returned false but left c1obstacle = true and HC as an
empty BRepAdaptor_Curve2d. PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine then took the obstacle path
(RstRst / CS walk) and evaluated the empty curve: access violation in
Geom2dAdaptor_Curve::EvalD0 (BRepBlend_RstRstConstRad::Value).

Now that branch clears c1obstacle and HC, like the other "no neighbour" returns:
the walk continues with the tangent plane or stops with "Chaining is impossible"
(a Standard_Failure the caller reports), instead of crashing.

Found by the downstream check of issue 031 round 2: a second fillet of a long
concave edge that ends in a flanked fillet corner (issue 5829 model) crashed the
stock TKFillet with 0xC0000005; with this change it is NOTDONE, as on the stock
corner. No other result changed in the DRAW blend group or in the own sweeps.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
index 9a6c5801..67d46717 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -1557,6 +1557,10 @@ bool ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol(
         }
         else
         {
+          // the arc is not found on the neighbour face: there is no obstacle to follow. HC
+          // must not stay an empty curve flagged as an obstacle (the walk would evaluate it)
+          c1obstacle = false;
+          HC.Nullify();
           prepareDefaultReturn();
           return false;
         }
